    "title": "BJ's Wholesale Club looks to open new store at former Walmart location in Towson - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chris Montcalmo ,\n12 hours ago TOWSON, MD—For several months now, residents in the Towson area have been wondering what will become of the former Walmart location at 1238 Putty Hill Avenue.\nWalmart said it closed the 155,000 square-foot space more than one year ago due to “performance issues.”\nNow, it appears that BJ’s Wholesale Club is looking to open a new storefront in its place.\nConstruction should begin sometime in 2027, pending various approvals from\nCounty.\nBJ’s says it hopes to open the new location sometime in 2028.",
